 \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 32 + 156 + 0 + 0 - (0 + 0 + 0 + 32) \\right|\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 188 - 32 \\right|\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 156 = 78\n\\]\n\nThe correct area of quadrilateral $DEGF$ is 78, not 288. This suggests there might be an error in the problem statement or our interpretation of it. Let's proceed to calculate the area of the heptagon $AFNBCEM$ using the coordinates of all vertices.\n\nThe coordinates of the vertices of the heptagon are $(0,0)$, $(4,0)$, $(12,8)$, $(0,13)$, $(0,8)$, $(4,-16)$, and $(12,-13)$. We can use the shoelace formula again to find the area of the heptagon:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 \\cdot 0 + 4 \\cdot 8 + 12 \\cdot 13 + 0 \\cdot 8 + 0 \\cdot 13 + 4 \\cdot -16 + 12 \\cdot -13 - (0 \\cdot 4 + 0 \\cdot 12 + 8 \\cdot 0 + 13 \\cdot 0 + 8 \\cdot 4 + 13 \\cdot 12 + -16 \\cdot -13) \\right|\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 0 + 32 + 156 + 0 + 0 - 64 + 156 - (0 + 0 + 0 + 0 + 32 + 156 + 208) \\right|\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} \\left| 384 - 428 \\right|\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 44 = 22\n\\]\n\nThe area of the heptagon $AFNBCEM$ is $22$. Therefore, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{22}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this with Python code to ensure the accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the coordinates of the vertices of the heptagon\nvertices = [(0,0), (4,0), (12,8), (0,13), (0,8), (4,-16), (12,-13)]\n\n# Function to calculate the area using the shoelace formula\ndef shoelace_formula(vertices):\n    n = len(vertices)\n    area = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        x1, y1 = vertices[i]\n        x2, y2 = vertices[(i + 1) % n]\n        area += x1 * y2 - y1 * x2\n    return abs(area) / 2\n\n# Calculate the area of the heptagon\narea_heptagon = shoelace_formula(vertices)\nprint(area_heptagon)\n```",
